drone_geolocation.py
------------------------------------------------------------------------

drone_geolocation.py is a Python port of src/renderMap.js from Roboflow's
dji-aerial-georeferencing project:

    https://github.com/roboflow/dji-aerial-georeferencing

That project is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of
the Apache License is included in this repository as LICENSE-APACHE-2.0,
and may also be obtained at:

    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The following are carried over from renderMap.js:

  - deriving the ground distance covered by a video frame from the
    camera's diagonal field of view and the drone's altitude
  - projecting a detection's pixel offset from frame center into a
    bearing and distance from the drone, then to a GPS coordinate along
    a rhumb line
  - merging repeat detections of the same subject by averaging their
    positions, and confirming a marker only once enough frames agree
  - the CONFIG thresholds MIN_SEPARATION_OF_DETECTIONS_IN_METERS (20)
    and MIN_DETECTIONS_TO_MAKE_VISIBLE (3), and their values

drone_geolocation.py has been modified from the original. The changes are:

  - rewritten from JavaScript into Python
  - Turf.js rhumbDestination() and distance() reimplemented locally as
    rhumb_destination() and haversine_distance_km()
  - Mapbox GL replaced with Folium for map rendering
  - Roboflow's hosted inference API replaced with a local Ultralytics
    YOLO checkpoint, behind a pluggable DetectionModel interface
  - flight-log parsing rewritten around pandas
  - per-detection snapshot capture added, which the original does not have

